{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/publication.cljc\ncat src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/publication.cljc\ncat src/cljc/yang/php/antlr/eval_publication.cljc'","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.php.antlr.publication\n  \"P6 (docs/design/yang.php.md section 11): a set of compiled PHP units\n   published as linker modules. The ordering, SCC bundling and publish loop\n   are `yang.core.publication`'s; this namespace supplies the PHP hooks: the\n   includes `lower/imported-unit-names` folds, the `lower/module-spec` and\n   `lower/scc-module-specs` emitters and site sets; no binder table.\n\n   A unit is `{:name path :packet p :strict-types b}`, `path` its normalized\n   relative path; the optional class map entry is `{:name \\\"$classmap\\\"\n   :classes {class path} :paths [path ...]}`. Name assertions stay the\n   linker's: this namespace publishes content, it signs nothing.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.core.publication :as core]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.siteset :as siteset]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]))\n\n\n(defn- class-map?\n  \"The autoload class map entry of a unit set, `{:name \\\"$classmap\\\" :classes\n   {class path} :paths [path ...]}`: it imports every path it lists, so it\n   publishes last and an unpublished path is refused by name (plan P6 R9).\"\n  [unit]\n  (= lower/classmap-name (:name unit)))\n\n\n(defn- config\n  [publish-fn]\n  {:imported-names (fn [{:keys [name packet], :as unit}]\n                     (if (class-map? unit)\n                       (lower/classmap-paths unit)\n                       (lower/imported-unit-names packet {:path name}))),\n   :module-spec (fn [registry {:keys [name packet strict-types], :as unit} php-address deps]\n                  (if (class-map? unit)\n                    (lower/classmap-spec registry unit php-address deps)\n                    (lower/module-spec registry packet\n                                       {:path name,\n                                        :strict-types strict-types,\n                                        :php-address php-address,\n                                        :deps deps}))),\n   :scc-module-specs lower/scc-module-specs,\n   :site-set siteset/publish!,\n   :alias-site-set true,\n   :binder-table nil,\n   :refusal-ns \"yang.php\",\n   :publish-fn publish-fn})\n\n\n(defn publication-order\n  \"Dependency-first names, retaining the input order for acyclic units.\n   Cyclic components appear as sorted member vectors in :order, one\n   publication step per SCC. An include edge no unit and no `published`\n   entry supplies is refused `:yang.php/unpublished-import` by name.\"\n  [units published]\n  (core/publication-order (config publish/publish-module!) units published))\n\n\n(defn publish-units!\n  \"Publish `units` into the content store `handle` over the host registry\n   `registry`, `php` pinned at `php-address` and each include outside the\n   set at its address in `published` ({path address}), in\n   `publication-order`. Answers `{:status :ok :addresses {path address}\n   :bundles {bundle-symbol address}}`, or the first refusal:\n   `publication-order`'s before anything is written, else\n   `publish-module!`'s with a string `:unit`.\"\n  ([handle registry php-address units]\n   (publish-units! handle registry php-address units {}))\n  ([handle registry php-address units published]\n   (publish-units! handle registry php-address units published publish/publish-module!))\n  ([handle registry php-address units published publish-fn]\n   (core/publish-units! (config publish-fn) handle registry php-address units published)))\n(ns yang.python.antlr.publication\n  \"C4 slices I3 and I5 (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6): a set of compiled Python\n   units published as linker modules. The ordering, SCC bundling and publish\n   loop are `yang.core.publication`'s; this namespace supplies the Python\n   hooks: the imports `lower/imported-module-names` hoists, the\n   `lower/module-spec` and `lower/scc-module-specs` emitters, the I7 site\n   set, and no binder table. Every Python module pins the `yang.call`\n   address from the published `py` module's requirements because its\n   runtime call path uses that dispatcher.\n   Name assertions stay the linker's (`yin.vm.linker.publish/assertion`\n   and `name-envelopes`): this namespace publishes content, it signs\n   nothing.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yang.core.publication :as core]\n            [yang.python.antlr.lower :as lower]\n            [yang.python.antlr.siteset :as siteset]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]))\n\n\n(defn- unit-imports\n  \"The Python modules unit `u` statically imports.\"\n  [{:keys [name package? packet]}]\n  (lower/imported-module-names packet\n                               {:name name, :package? (boolean package?)}))\n\n\n(defn- config\n  [publish-fn call-address]\n  {:imported-names unit-imports,\n   :module-spec (fn [registry {:keys [name package? packet]} py-address deps]\n                  (lower/module-spec registry packet\n                                     {:name name, :package? package?,\n                                      :py-address py-address, :call-address call-address,\n                                      :deps deps})),\n   :scc-module-specs (fn [registry units py-address deps]\n                       (lower/scc-module-specs registry units py-address call-address deps)),\n   :site-set siteset/publish!,\n   :binder-table nil,\n   :refusal-ns \"yang.python.antlr\",\n   :publish-fn publish-fn})\n\n\n(defn publication-order\n  \"Dependency-first names, retaining the I3 order for acyclic units.\n   Cyclic components appear as sorted member vectors in :order, one\n   publication step per SCC. External imports must be in `published`.\"\n  [units published]\n  (core/publication-order (config publish/publish-module! nil) units published))\n\n\n(defn publish-units!\n  \"Publish `units` (`[{:name :package? :packet}]`) into the content store\n   `handle` over the host registry `registry`, `py` pinned at\n   `py-address` and each import outside the set at its address in\n   `published` ({python-name address}), in `publication-order`. Answers\n   `{:status :ok :addresses {python-name address}\n     :bundles {bundle-symbol address}\n     :sites {python-name-or-bundle-symbol site-publication}}` for the units\n   of the set (`siteset/publish!`'s answer for each module published beside\n   its code image, I7; an SCC member alias carries no marks and so no\n   entry, its bundle does). The publisher that asserts these names\n   indexes `siteset/signed-entries` of `:sites` in the same index\n   transaction; a module whose entry is missing is refused by every\n   hook-profile reader. Or the\n   first refusal: `publication-order`'s before anything is written, else\n   `publish-module!`'s with a string `:unit`: the Python name for a member,\n   or the bundle module name for an SCC bundle. Every bundle name must be\n   asserted/bound alongside the member names for aliases to deliver.\n   Optional `publish-fn` takes `[handle spec]`, defaulting to\n   `publish/publish-module!`, for both bundles and members.\"\n  ([handle registry py-address units]\n   (publish-units! handle registry py-address units {}))\n  ([handle registry py-address units published]\n   (publish-units! handle registry py-address units published publish/publish-module!))\n  ([handle registry py-address units published publish-fn]\n   (let [py-manifest (when (and handle py-address)\n                       (jing/get handle py-address nil))\n         call-address (get-in py-manifest [:yin.module/requires 'yang.call])]\n     (core/publish-units! (config publish-fn call-address)\n                          handle registry py-address units published))))\n(ns yang.php.antlr.eval-publication\n  \"Publish an admitted eval unit and its canonical safepoint occurrences.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n            [yang.php.antlr.siteset :as siteset]\n            [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]))\n\n\n(defn publish!\n  \"Publish a prepared, successfully parsed eval unit under the supplied name.\n   Retain the coordinator's identity and bind its site set to the manifest.\"\n  [store registry name prepared]\n  (if (= :yang.cst/ok (get-in prepared [:cst :yang.cst/outcome]))\n    (let [spec (lower/eval-module-spec registry name (:cst prepared)\n                                       {:eval-service? (boolean (module/module-entry (:modules registry)\n                                                                                     'eval.compiler))})\n          result (publish/publish-module! store spec)]\n      (if (= :refused (:status result))\n        result\n        (assoc result :status :ok :identity (:identity prepared)\n               :source-address (jing/materialize! store (:identity prepared))\n               :sites (siteset/publish! store (:address result) (:ast spec)))))\n    {:status :refused :reason :eval-source-not-ready :identity (:identity prepared)}))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
