{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/agents/malleability.md | sed -n '76,154p'\nnl -ba collab/exception-track/1794852821344-dry-r2-full.patch.txt | sed -n '1,120p'\"","aggregated_output":"    76\t### Public vs. Private: Minimize Interface Surface Area\n    77\t\n    78\tAny function without external dependencies should be marked private.\n    79\t\n    80\t**The rule:**\n    81\t- Mark a function **private** (`defn-`) if it is called only from within its own namespace.\n    82\t- Mark a function **public** (`defn`) only if it is called from other namespaces.\n    83\t\n    84\tThis keeps the public API surface minimal. Callers see only what they need; internal implementation details stay hidden. The public interface becomes self-documenting: what's exposed is what the namespace is *for*.\n    85\t\n    86\t**How to verify external callers:**\n    87\t\n    88\tFor any public function, check if it's called from outside its namespace:\n    89\t\n    90\t```bash\n    91\tgrep -r \"namespace-name/function-name\" src/\n    92\t```\n    93\t\n    94\t**Interpretation:**\n    95\t- **0 results**: The function has no external callers. Mark it private (`defn-`) or delete it.\n    96\t- **Only matches in its own file**: The function is called only internally. Mark it private (`defn-`).\n    97\t- **Matches in other files**: The function has external callers. Keep it public.\n    98\t\n    99\t**Example:**\n   100\t```bash\n   101\tgrep -r \"yin.vm/load-program\" src/\n   102\t# If this returns results outside yin/vm/*, the function is used externally\n   103\t# If only results are in yin/vm/*, or if grep returns nothing, mark it private\n   104\t```\n   105\t\n   106\t**Measure:**\n   107\tCount the public functions (see \"Bounded Complexity\" for the 2-5 entry point target). If the count is high, either more functions should be private, or the namespace is doing too many things and needs to be split.\n   108\t\n   109\t## Workflow: Start Messy, Let Structure Emerge\n   110\t\n   111\t1. Write everything in one namespace. Don't organize prematurely.\n   112\t2. Explore behavior in REPL `(comment ...)` blocks.\n   113\t3. Observe which functions depend on each other: call each other, share data shapes, appear together in tests, or are always imported as a unit.\n   114\t4. Extract cohesive clusters into separate namespaces when boundaries become clear. Extract them together to keep related changes local.\n   115\t5. Delete stale comment blocks ruthlessly.\n   116\t6. Iterate as requirements change.\n   117\t\n   118\t(See \"Selection Pressure\" for testing strategy.)\n   119\t\n   120\t### When to Extract: Extraction Trigger and Signals\n   121\t\n   122\t**Trigger**: When a namespace reaches ~12 functions, evaluate whether extraction is needed.\n   123\t\n   124\t**Signals of a natural cluster**:\n   125\t- Functions call each other (high internal coupling)\n   126\t- Rarely called from outside (low external coupling)\n   127\t- Appear together in tests\n   128\t- Work with the same data structures\n   129\t- Share the exact same set of external dependencies (structural clustering)\n   130\t\n   131\t**Extract when**: The structure has already emerged in your code. You're just formalizing what exists, not designing from scratch.\n   132\t\n   133\t**Naming**: Use problem domain names (`validation`, `auth`, `indexing`), not solution domain (`utils`, `helpers`). See docs/agents/vocabulary.md for vocabulary from biology, economics, physics, philosophy.\n     1\tdiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/core/lower.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/core/lower.cljc\n     2\tindex f5d8b096..32e8f30f 100644\n     3\t--- a/src/cljc/yang/core/lower.cljc\n     4\t+++ b/src/cljc/yang/core/lower.cljc\n     5\t@@ -97,3 +97,15 @@\n     6\t                      (and (not (contains? stop (:rule k)))\n     7\t                           (contains-rule? ctx k rule-name stop)))))\n     8\t           (kids ctx n))))\n     9\t+\n    10\t+\n    11\t+(defn code-point->str\n    12\t+  [cp]\n    13\t+  #?(:cljd (let [sb (StringBuffer)] (.writeCharCode sb cp) (.toString sb))\n    14\t+     :clj (String. (Character/toChars (int cp)))\n    15\t+     :cljs (.fromCodePoint js/String cp)))\n    16\t+\n    17\t+\n    18\t+(defn build-vector\n    19\t+  [vconj elems]\n    20\t+  (reduce (fn [acc e] (app* vconj acc e)) (u/lit []) elems))\n    21\tdiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc\n    22\tindex ee928753..c2085d49 100644\n    23\t--- a/src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc\n    24\t+++ b/src/cljc/yang/core/prelude.cljc\n    25\t@@ -175,3 +175,19 @@\n    26\t                       (refusal refusal-ns \"host-names\"\n    27\t                                {(keyword refusal-ns \"missing\") missing}))))\n    28\t     registry))\n    29\t+\n    30\t+\n    31\t+(defn balanced-definitions->uast\n    32\t+  [defs]\n    33\t+  (letfn [(sequence-tree [nodes]\n    34\t+            (if (<= (count nodes) 1)\n    35\t+              (first nodes)\n    36\t+              (let [middle (quot (count nodes) 2)]\n    37\t+                (u/then (sequence-tree (subvec nodes 0 middle))\n    38\t+                        (sequence-tree (subvec nodes middle))))))]\n    39\t+    (sequence-tree (mapv (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs))))\n    40\t+\n    41\t+\n    42\t+(defn definitions->uast\n    43\t+  [defs]\n    44\t+  (u/seq-nodes (map (fn [[k form]] (u/def! k (u/sexp->uast form))) defs)))\n    45\tdiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/core/siteset_publication.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/core/siteset_publication.cljc\n    46\tnew file mode 100644\n    47\tindex 00000000..be123967\n    48\t--- /dev/null\n    49\t+++ b/src/cljc/yang/core/siteset_publication.cljc\n    50\t@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n    51\t+(ns yang.core.siteset-publication\n    52\t+  \"Shared signed site publication operations.\"\n    53\t+  (:require [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n    54\t+\n    55\t+\n    56\t+(defn signed-entry\n    57\t+  \"Sign the association between a published manifest and its site record.\"\n    58\t+  [key manifest record-address]\n    59\t+  (let [env {:yang.site/op :publish,\n    60\t+             :yang.site/manifest manifest,\n    61\t+             :yang.site/record record-address,\n    62\t+             :yin.module/asserted-by (sign/principal (:public key))}]\n    63\t+    {:envelope env, :proof (sign/sign-envelope (:seed key) env)}))\n    64\t+\n    65\t+\n    66\t+(defn entry-datoms\n    67\t+  \"Index signed site publications alongside name assertions.\"\n    68\t+  [signed]\n    69\t+  (vec (mapcat (fn [e {:keys [envelope proof]}]\n    70\t+                 [[e :yang.site/envelope envelope]\n    71\t+                  [e :yang.site/proof proof]])\n    72\t+               (range) signed)))\n    73\t+\n    74\t+\n    75\t+(defn signed-entries\n    76\t+  \"Sign all site publications returned by unit publication, including aliases.\"\n    77\t+  [publisher sites addresses bundles]\n    78\t+  (mapv (fn [[k s]]\n    79\t+          (signed-entry publisher (or (get addresses k) (get bundles k))\n    80\t+                        (:record-address s)))\n    81\t+        (sort-by (comp str key) sites)))\n    82\tdiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/core/siteset_store.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/core/siteset_store.cljc\n    83\tnew file mode 100644\n    84\tindex 00000000..9a02e7b3\n    85\t--- /dev/null\n    86\t+++ b/src/cljc/yang/core/siteset_store.cljc\n    87\t@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@\n    88\t+(ns yang.core.siteset-store\n    89\t+  \"Shared tree loading and buffered store operations.\"\n    90\t+  (:require [yin.vm :as vm]))\n    91\t+\n    92\t+\n    93\t+(defn load-tree\n    94\t+  \"The canonical row set `{:root :rows}` of the tree at `root` in `handle`,\n    95\t+   every row fetched by its address, depth-first: `{:status :missing\n    96\t+   :address a}` for the first row the handle does not hold, nil when a row\n    97\t+   is not its address or no tree row.\"\n    98\t+  [read-at absent? handle root]\n    99\t+  (loop [todo [root]\n   100\t+         rows {}]\n   101\t+    (if-let [id (peek todo)]\n   102\t+      (if (contains? rows id)\n   103\t+        (recur (pop todo) rows)\n   104\t+        (let [body (read-at handle id)\n   105\t+              slots (when (vector? body)\n   106\t+                      (get vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar (first body)))]\n   107\t+          (cond\n   108\t+            (absent? body) {:status :missing, :address id}\n   109\t+            slots (recur (into (pop todo)\n   110\t+                               (mapcat (fn [[_ kind] v]\n   111\t+                                         (case kind\n   112\t+                                           :node [v]\n   113\t+                                           :nodes v\n   114\t+                                           nil))\n   115\t+                                       slots\n   116\t+                                       (rest body)))\n   117\t+                         (assoc rows id (into [id] body)))\n   118\t+            :else nil)))\n   119\t+      {:root root, :rows rows})))\n   120\t+\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
